# Gossip, debts and promises, the people one deals with (priest, shopkeeper, leader, neighbour), the realm's figures,
# and the town's news (theme n7). Each opener remembers what it was about (pair.mem.on, and its own key), the other
# answers as they are and remembers how they took it, and the opener has the last word (town.close).
#
# Gossip: topic.claim is whatever was heard ("died", "married", "is new in town", "keeps promises", "stole from Hild",
# "was robbed by someone they couldn't make out"...). Only the one-word claims can be tested, so a death and a
# wedding have their own lines; everything else is told and taken in words that suit good news and bad.

## Gossip, told as the teller is (talk.gossip: topic.subject, topic.claim)

rule n7_go_sly
when concept=talk.gossip self.honesty=sly
cooldown 1d
say I shouldn't say. But I will. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Now, you didn't hear this from me: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I know something you don't. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Worth a drink, that.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_chatty
when concept=talk.gossip self.talk=chatty
cooldown 1d
say Oh, you'll love this. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#! | Sit down, sit down. You'll never guess. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Have you heard? You haven't! #topic.subject# #topic.claim#!
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_devout
when concept=talk.gossip self.piety=devout
cooldown 1d
say I don't hold with tattle. But you ought to know. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I'll say it once and say no more: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | It was all the talk after chapel. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_quiet
when concept=talk.gossip self.talk=quiet
cooldown 1d
say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's all I'll say. | Heard something. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#, they say. | Mm. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Thought you'd want to know.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_nervy
when concept=talk.gossip self.temper=nervy
cooldown 1d
say Don't look round. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'm not saying it's true. | I'm only saying what I heard. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Don't tell anyone I said. | Is anyone listening? Right. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_neighbours
when concept=talk.gossip pair.neighbours=yes
cooldown 1d
say The whole row's talking. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Over the back wall this morning: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | You'll not have heard, you were out. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_chapel
when concept=talk.gossip here.place=chapel
cooldown 1d
say Not here. Well, quickly: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | The whole back pew knows. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Lean in. Quietly. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_tavern
when concept=talk.gossip here.place=tavern
cooldown 1d
say Lean in. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Straight from behind the bar. | Another jug and I'll tell you. No, I'll tell you now: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | The whole room's buzzing. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_old
when concept=talk.gossip self.stage=old
cooldown 1d
say I've seen a lot of years, and this one's new to me. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | You young ones won't credit it. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Now then. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. What do you make of that?
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_young
when concept=talk.gossip self.stage=young|adolescent
cooldown 1d
say #mum# says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#! Is that bad? | The big pups at the well say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I heard the grown-ups. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#! I'm not supposed to know.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_servant
when concept=talk.gossip self.job=servant
cooldown 1d
say You hear things, serving at table. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | The household's talked of nothing else. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | They forget we've ears. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_guard
when concept=talk.gossip self.role=guard
cooldown 1d
say I shouldn't, being the Watch. But #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | It came up at the watch post. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Word among the Watch: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_merchant
when concept=talk.gossip self.role=merchant here.place=market|work
cooldown 1d
say Every customer today, same story. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Sold more gossip than goods this morning. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | A counter hears everything. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_rivals
when concept=talk.gossip pair.band=rivals
cooldown 1d
say I suppose even you should hear this. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Thought you'd know already, you know everything. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Here's something you didn't know first: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_spouses
when concept=talk.gossip pair.band=spouses
cooldown 1d
say #dear.capitalize#, you'll never guess. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Don't make that face. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Guess what I heard at the well. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_married
when concept=talk.gossip topic.claim=married
cooldown 1d
say #topic.subject#'s married! Did you know? | Well, #topic.subject#'s gone and married. | Wedding bells for #topic.subject#. Who'd have thought it?
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_died
when concept=talk.gossip topic.claim=died
priority 10
cooldown 1d
say Did you hear? #topic.subject# died. | #topic.subject#'s gone. Died, they said. I can't take it in. | They're saying #topic.subject# died. Is it true?
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_died_old
when concept=talk.gossip topic.claim=died self.stage=old
priority 10
cooldown 1d
say #topic.subject#'s gone. Another one. They're dropping like leaves this year. | Have you heard about #topic.subject#? Died. I'd have bet on me going first. | #topic.subject# died. I remember them as a pup, tumbling in the street.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

rule n7_go_died_warm
when concept=talk.gossip topic.claim=died self.warmth=warm
priority 10
cooldown 1d
say Oh, have you heard? #topic.subject#. They died. I can't stop thinking about it. | I've had sad news. #topic.subject# died. | It's #topic.subject#. They've died. I keep wanting to go round with a pie.
remember pair: on=gossip 1h
then other: town.gossip

## Hearing it (self is the one told)

rule n7_ga2_plain
when concept=town.gossip
say #topic.subject#? Never. | Who told you that? | Well, I never. | Is that so? Well, well.
remember pair: ha=plain 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_plain2
when concept=town.gossip
say #surprise#. | Huh. Fancy that. | Hm. | Mm.

rule n7_ga2_frank
when concept=town.gossip self.honesty=frank
say I'll ask #topic.subject# myself, then. | I'll believe it when I hear it from #topic.subject#. | Then I'll hear it from #topic.subject#, not from the well.
remember pair: ha=doubt 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_guarded
when concept=town.gossip self.honesty=guarded
say I'd not repeat that, if I were you. | Hm. I'll keep that to myself. | I didn't hear it. Nor did you.
remember pair: ha=hush 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_sly
when concept=town.gossip self.honesty=sly
say And? There's always more. What else? | Interesting. Who else knows? | That's worth knowing. Thank you. Very much.
remember pair: ha=eager 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_chatty
when concept=town.gossip self.talk=chatty
say No! Wait till I tell my sister. | I knew it! Didn't I say? I said! | Tell me everything. Slowly. From the start.
remember pair: ha=eager 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_warm
when concept=town.gossip self.warmth=warm topic.claim!=married
say Oh. Well, I hope they're all right, whatever's what. | I'll call on #topic.subject#. See how they are. | We shouldn't talk. But oh, #topic.subject#.
remember pair: ha=kind 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_cold
when concept=town.gossip self.warmth=cold
say Not my business. | And? | Doesn't surprise me.
remember pair: ha=cold 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_devout
when concept=town.gossip self.piety=devout topic.claim!=married
say The gods hear tattle too, you know. | Judge not. Well. A little. | I'll pray for #topic.subject#. And for us, for listening.
remember pair: ha=pious 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_guard
when concept=town.gossip self.role=guard topic.claim!=married
say I'll keep an ear open. | I'll make a note of that. | Hm. I'll keep my eye on #topic.subject#.
remember pair: ha=plain 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_priest
when concept=town.gossip self.job=priest topic.claim!=married
say I'll not hear it. And nor should you. | If #topic.subject# needs help, I'll go. If not, I'll not hear another word. | Words are stones. Be careful where you throw them.
remember pair: ha=pious 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_old
when concept=town.gossip self.stage=old
say I've heard it all in my time. Most of it twice. | It'll be forgotten by the next festival. Everything is. | Ha. Their grandmother was just the same.
remember pair: ha=plain 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_young
when concept=town.gossip self.stage=young
say What does that mean? | Is that bad? It sounds bad. | I'm telling everyone!
remember pair: ha=pup 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_dry
when concept=town.gossip self.humour=dry
say And the moon's made of cheese, I suppose. | Gossip travels fast. The truth's still putting its boots on. | Fascinating. Tell me again, slower, so I can not believe it properly.
remember pair: ha=doubt 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_merry
when concept=town.gossip self.humour=merry
say Ha! No! | Oh, that's too good. Is it true? Don't tell me. Tell me. | Ha! I'll never look at #topic.subject# the same.
remember pair: ha=eager 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_nervy
when concept=town.gossip self.temper=nervy
say Don't. If they hear we said it... | Shh! Not so loud. | Oh, I wish you hadn't told me. Now I'll have to not tell people.
remember pair: ha=hush 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_married
when concept=town.gossip topic.claim=married
say Good for them. | Married! Well, well. Who to? | About time, I'd say. | Married? I'll believe it when I see the cake.
remember pair: ha=glad 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_married_warm
when concept=town.gossip topic.claim=married self.warmth=warm
say Oh, that's lovely. I'll take them something. | Bless them. Bless them both. | Oh! I do love a wedding.
remember pair: ha=glad 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_married_dry
when concept=town.gossip topic.claim=married self.humour=dry
say Married. They'll learn. | Poor soul. Whichever one it is. | Married. Well. Somebody had to.
remember pair: ha=glad 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_death
when concept=town.gossip topic.claim=died
priority 3
say Gods. I'd no idea. | No. I saw them only the other day. | Dead? #topic.subject#? Oh, that's hard.
remember pair: ha=dead 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_death_devout
when concept=town.gossip topic.claim=died self.piety=devout
priority 3
say The Bright One keep them. I'll light a candle tonight. | May they find their rest. | We'll pray for them at Restday. All of us.
remember pair: ha=dead 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_death_old
when concept=town.gossip topic.claim=died self.stage=old
priority 3
say They go so fast now. All of them. | It's never the right ones. | Another. I'll be next, mark me.
remember pair: ha=dead 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_ga2_death_cold
when concept=town.gossip topic.claim=died self.warmth=cold
priority 3
say Hm. Everyone goes. | I hardly knew them. | Well. That's that.
remember pair: ha=dead 1h
then other: town.close

## The last word on gossip (the teller; pair.mem.ha says how it was taken)

rule n7_close_go
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=gossip
say Well. That's what they're saying. | I'm only telling you what I heard. | Make of it what you like.

rule n7_close_go_doubt
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=gossip pair.mem.ha=doubt
say Suit yourself. You'll see. | Believe what you like. I know what I heard. | Ask anyone.

rule n7_close_go_hush
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=gossip pair.mem.ha=hush
say Not a word, then. | You're right. Forget I said it. | My lips are sealed. From now.

rule n7_close_go_eager
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=gossip pair.mem.ha=eager
say That's all I know. Honest. | I'll tell you the rest when I have it. | I knew you'd like that one.

rule n7_close_go_eager_sly
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=gossip pair.mem.ha=eager self.honesty=sly
say There's more, but it'll cost you a drink. | Keep it close. It's worth more that way. | Remember: you heard it here first.

rule n7_close_go_kind
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=gossip pair.mem.ha=kind
say Aye. Let's hope so. | You're kinder than most. | You're right. We shouldn't.

rule n7_close_go_cold
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=gossip pair.mem.ha=cold
say Please yourself. | I only thought you'd want to know. | Fine. I'll tell someone who cares.

rule n7_close_go_pious
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=gossip pair.mem.ha=pious
say I know. I know. Gods forgive me. | I'll say no more of it. | You're right. I'll say a prayer for loose tongues. Mine first.

rule n7_close_go_pup
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=gossip pair.mem.ha=pup
say Never you mind. And don't repeat it! | Hush now. Forget I said. | Not bad. Just grown-up business.

rule n7_close_go_glad
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=gossip pair.mem.ha=glad
say There'll be a feast, I'd think. | It's nice to hear good news for once. | I'll find out who to, don't you worry.

rule n7_close_go_death
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=gossip pair.mem.ha=dead
say Aye. Gone, just like that. | I'll miss seeing them about. | It makes you think.

## Debts and promises between the two (pair.owed and pair.promise name the one who owes, the one who promised)

rule n7_db_dun
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.friends pair.owed=b
cooldown 2d
say About that money you owe me... | Not to rush you, but it's been a while. You know what I mean. | I don't like to ask. I'm asking.
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=dun 1h
then other: town.debt

rule n7_db_dun_short
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.owed=b self.temper=short
cooldown 2d
say Where's my money? | You owe me. Don't pretend you've forgotten. | I've been patient. I'm done being patient.
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=dun 1h
then other: town.debt

rule n7_db_dun_poor
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.owed=b self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
priority 1
say I'd not ask, but I need what you owe me. | I'm #skint#, #address#. Even a little of what you owe would help. | I've not eaten since yesterday. That money. Please.
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=dun 1h
then other: town.debt

rule n7_db_pay
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.friends pair.owed=a
cooldown 2d
say I've not forgotten what I owe you. Restday, I swear. | Here's some of it. The rest when I can. | I know, I know. I owe you. I've not forgotten.
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=pay 1h
then other: town.debt

rule n7_db_pay_sly
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.owed=a self.honesty=sly
cooldown 2d
say Before you say anything: lovely day, isn't it? | You're looking well! Very well! Prosperous, even. | Friend! Old friend! Have I told you how much I value you?
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=flatter 1h
then other: town.debt

rule n7_db_promise_due
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.friends pair.promise=b
cooldown 2d
say You said you'd give me a paw with the roof. | Still coming Restday, like you promised? | I'm holding you to your word, you know.
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=promised 1h
then other: town.debt

rule n7_db_promise_mine
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.friends pair.promise=a
cooldown 2d
say I've not forgotten my promise. I'll be round. | What I said I'd do, I'll do. Give me till Restday. | I gave you my word. That's that.
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=promising 1h
then other: town.debt

rule n7_db_word_bad
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.rumour=breaks_promises
cooldown 3d
priority 1
say Folk say your word's worth nothing. Tell me they're wrong. | I heard you let someone down. Badly. | They say if you promise something, start counting the days.
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=word_bad 1h
then other: town.debt

rule n7_db_word_good
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.rumour=keeps_promises
cooldown 3d
say They say when you give your word it's iron. I need a wolf like that. | I hear you're as good as your word. Rare, that. | Folk say you keep your promises. Is that so?
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=word_good 1h
then other: town.debt

rule n7_db_lend_ask
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.friends self.owes=yes pair.band=friends|family self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 3d
say You couldn't lend me a little? Only till Restday. | I'm in a hole, #pet#. A small loan would get me out. | I hate this. Could you spare me a few pennies?
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=lend 1h
then other: town.debt

rule n7_db_slate_ask
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.prices pair.customer=a self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say Could you put it on my slate? Just this week. | I'll pay Restday. Can I take it now? | You know I'm good for it. Mostly.
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=slate 1h
then other: town.debt

rule n7_db_slate_due
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.prices pair.customer=b other.owes=yes
cooldown 2d
say Your slate's getting long, #address#. | I've a tally here with your name on it. A long one. | I can't give more till something's paid off. I'm sorry.
remember pair: on=debt 1h
remember pair: db=slate_due 1h
then other: town.debt

## Answering about money and promises (each remembers its stance, pair.mem.da)

rule n7_da_plain
when concept=town.debt
say Aye. I know. | Fair enough. | Right. Restday, then.
remember pair: da=promise 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_dun
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=dun
say Restday. I swear it. | I've not forgotten. Give me a few days. | I know. I'm ashamed. Month's end, every penny.
remember pair: da=promise 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_dun_poor
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=dun self.wealth=poor|destitute
say I've nothing. Take my coat, if you want it. | If I had it you'd have it. I swear. | Can you wait? Please. Just a little longer.
remember pair: da=plead 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_dun_rich
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=dun self.wealth=rich|comfortable
say Is it so much? Here. Take it now and we'll say no more. | Gods, I'd forgotten entirely. How embarrassing. Here. | Of course. With something for the wait.
regard other: trust +1
remember pair: da=paid 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_dun_sly
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=dun self.honesty=sly
say What money? Oh, that. Of course. Soon. | I thought we'd agreed that was a gift. | I paid you. Didn't I? I'm sure I did.
regard other: trust -1
remember pair: da=dodge 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_dun_short
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=dun self.temper=short
say You'll get it when you get it. | Don't badger me in the street. | I said I'd pay. Stop asking.
remember pair: da=bite 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_pay
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=pay
say I know you're good for it. | No rush. Well. Some rush. | That'll do. Pay when you can.
remember pair: da=ease 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_pay_warm
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=pay self.warmth=warm
say Don't fret over it. Pay when you can. | Keep it a while. You need it more. | Friends first, money after.
regard other: affinity +1
remember pair: da=ease 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_pay_rich
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=pay self.wealth=rich
say Keep it. Buy yourself something hot. | It's nothing. Truly. Forget it. | Half, then, and we'll call it square.
regard other: affinity +1
remember pair: da=ease 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_pay_cold
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=pay self.warmth=cold
say See that you do. | I've written it down. | Restday. Not the one after.
remember pair: da=stern 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_flatter
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=flatter
say And my money? | Very nice. Where's what you owe me? | You only talk like that when you owe me.
remember pair: da=stern 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_flatter_warm
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=flatter self.warmth=warm
say Ha. I know what you're doing. Pay me Restday and I'll forget it. | Flattery and no pennies. Typical. | Go on with you. I know you're good for it. Eventually.
remember pair: da=ease 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_promised
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=promised
say I said I would and I will. | Restday. I've not forgotten. | My word's my word.
remember pair: da=promise 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_promised_sly
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=promised self.honesty=sly
say Did I say this Restday? | Help, yes. I didn't say how much help. | Something came up. Something will always come up, I'm afraid.
regard other: trust -1
remember pair: da=dodge 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_promised_nervy
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=promised self.temper=nervy
say Oh gods. I forgot. I'm sorry. I'm so sorry. | I'll be there! I will! What day did I say? | I haven't forgotten. I had forgotten. I've remembered now.
remember pair: da=promise 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_promising
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=promising
say I'll hold you to it. | Good. I'll have the kettle on. | Don't make me come looking.
remember pair: da=ease 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_word_bad
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=word_bad
say They're wrong. | One time. One time, and the town never forgets. | Who's been talking?
remember pair: da=deny 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_word_bad_short
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=word_bad self.temper=short
say Say that again and see what I keep. | Who said that? Name them. | I keep my word to those who deserve it.
regard self: affinity -1
remember pair: da=bite 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_word_good
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=word_good
say I keep it when I can. What is it you need? | What I say, I do. Simple as that. | My father taught me. Say less, do more.
regard other: trust +1
remember pair: da=assure 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_lend
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=lend
say Here. Don't make me ask for it back. | I can spare a little. Not a lot. Here. | Here's what I have on me. Restday, mind.
regard other: affinity +1
remember pair: da=give 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_lend_cold
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=lend self.warmth=cold
say I don't lend to friends. Keeps them friends. | No. Sorry. No. | Go to a moneylender. That's what they're for.
remember pair: da=refuse 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_lend_poor
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=lend self.wealth=poor|destitute
say I'm as #skint# as you are. | I've three pennies. Want one? | If I had it. You know I would.
remember pair: da=none 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_slate
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=slate
say Just this week, mind. | Go on. I'll write it down. | Take it. Pay when you can.
regard other: affinity +1
remember pair: da=give 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_slate_failing
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=slate self.business=failing
priority 1
say I can't. I'm sorry. Half the street owes me already. | If I give credit to one more, I'll be on somebody's slate myself. | I'd love to. I can't. Look at my shelves.
remember pair: da=refuse 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_da_slate_due
when concept=town.debt pair.mem.db=slate_due
say I'll pay Restday. Every penny. | I know. I'm sorry. Things are tight. | Can I work it off? I can sweep, carry, anything.
remember pair: da=promise 1h
then other: town.close

## The last word on money and promises (pair.mem.da says how it was taken)

rule n7_close_debt
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt
say Right. | Well. We'll see. | Hm.

rule n7_close_debt_promise
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=promise
say Right. Restday, then. | I'll hold you to it. | Good. That's all I ask. | See that you do.

rule n7_close_debt_promise_warm
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=promise self.warmth=warm
say Don't lose sleep over it. | I know you will. | Good. Now, let's talk of something nicer.

rule n7_close_debt_plead
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=plead
say ...All right. Restday. Do your best. | Keep your coat. I'll wait. | We're both in a hole, then.

rule n7_close_debt_paid
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=paid
say Thank you. That's a weight off. | You're a good sort. | That'll see me through the week.

rule n7_close_debt_dodge
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=dodge
say Don't give me that. | I'll remember this. | Nice try. I'll be round Restday. | You know full well what you said.

rule n7_close_debt_bite
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=bite
say Hmph. Restday, then. And not a day after. | Don't take that tone with me. | Fine. I'll ask again tomorrow. And the day after.

rule n7_close_debt_ease
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=ease
say You're good to me. | Thank you. I'll not forget it. | I'll not keep you waiting long. | Restday. Truly.

rule n7_close_debt_stern
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=stern
say Restday. I swear. | I know. I know. | Gods, you'd have the pennies off a dead wolf's eyes.

rule n7_close_debt_deny
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=deny
say I hope that's so. | I'll judge for myself. | Then show me.

rule n7_close_debt_assure
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=assure
say Good. I may need you, then. | That's what I hoped to hear. | I'll come to you, then. Soon.

rule n7_close_debt_give
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=give
say Thank you. Truly. | You've saved me. | Restday. Every penny.

rule n7_close_debt_refuse
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=refuse
say Right. Forget I asked. | I understand. | I'll manage somehow.

rule n7_close_debt_none
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=debt pair.mem.da=none
say I know. Thank you anyway. | Keep your pennies. | We'll muddle through, the pair of us.

## The people they deal with: their priest, their shopkeeper, their leader, their neighbour by name

rule n7_ro_priest_devout
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day self.priest self.piety=devout pair.flock=no
cooldown 3d
say #self.priest# preached on charity last Restday. Half the front pews left early. | #self.priest# blessed our door. I feel safer. Is that silly? | Have you heard #self.priest# sing? Like a bell. A cracked bell, but a bell.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=priest 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_priest_ordinary
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day self.priest self.piety=ordinary pair.flock=no
cooldown 3d
say #self.priest# caught me nodding off in chapel. Again. | #self.priest# asked why I wasn't at chapel. I said my knees. My knees were at the tavern. | #self.priest# went on for an hour last Restday. An hour!
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=priest 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_to_priest
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.flock=b
cooldown 3d
say Will it be a long sermon this Restday? Only my knees. | I've been meaning to come and see you. About my sister. | Bless me, would you? I've a feeling about this week.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=to_priest 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_priest_to_flock
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.flock=a
cooldown 3d
say I've not seen you at chapel lately. | How's your soul, these days? I ask everyone. Nobody answers. | Come Restday. There's bread after, if nothing else.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=flock 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_priest_to_flock_poor
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day pair.flock=a other.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 3d
priority 1
say There's bread at the chapel door after the bell. Come. No questions. | The poor box isn't only for putting in. You know that? | If the rent's the trouble, come and talk to me. The chapel has a little.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=flock_poor 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_shopkeeper_short
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.prices self.shopkeeper pair.customer=no
cooldown 3d
say #self.shopkeeper# gave me short weight again. I'm sure of it. | Went to #self.shopkeeper#'s for candles. The price had grown legs. | #self.shopkeeper# never smiles. Not once in ten years.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=shop 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_shopkeeper_kind
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.prices self.shopkeeper self.warmth=warm pair.customer=no
cooldown 3d
say #self.shopkeeper# kept a loaf back for me. Didn't even ask. | #self.shopkeeper# let me off a penny. Said I'd an honest face. | Say what you like about #self.shopkeeper#, they'd give you the coat off their back. Then charge you for the buttons.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=shopgood 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_customer_ask
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.prices pair.customer=a
cooldown 2d
say Keep one back for me on Restday? | Got any of the good stuff in? The stuff you keep under the counter? | Put something by for me, would you? I'll be in tomorrow.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=customer 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_customer_price
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.prices pair.customer=a
cooldown 2d
say Is it up again? The price? Don't tell me. | What's it to be this week? Same as last, I pray. | Tell me it's not gone up again.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=customer_price 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_keeper_miss
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.prices pair.customer=b
cooldown 2d
say You've not been in this week. Found somewhere else? | Not seen you in a while. I was starting to worry. | You've gone off me, haven't you? Nine days without a visit.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=keeper_miss 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_keeper_offer
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.prices pair.customer=b
cooldown 2d
say Your usual's put by. Didn't even have to ask. | I've something new in. You'll want to see it. | Come by later. I've kept something back for you.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=keeper 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_leader
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.lore self.leader
cooldown 3d
say #self.leader#'s people were round counting doors. | #self.leader# rode past this morning. Didn't look left or right. | They say #self.leader# eats off silver every night. Every night!
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=leader 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_leader_house
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.work self.leader self.house self.wealth!=rich
cooldown 3d
say #self.leader# wants the books by Restday. Every page. | #self.leader# came down to the floor today. Everyone stood straighter. | You don't argue with #self.leader#. You nod, and then you do it.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=leader_house 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_neighbour_name
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day self.neighbour pair.neighbours=no
cooldown 3d
say #self.neighbour# next door's taken up the fiddle. Gods help me. | #self.neighbour#'s been at the wall again with a hammer. What are they building? | #self.neighbour# knows everything about everyone on our row. Everything.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=neighbour 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_ro_neighbour_kind
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day self.neighbour pair.neighbours=no self.warmth=warm
cooldown 3d
say #self.neighbour# brought round a pie when I was poorly. Good sort. | Lucky with my neighbour. #self.neighbour# keeps an eye on the place when I'm late. | #self.neighbour# and I share a wall and a stew-pot. Half each.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=neighbourgood 1h
then other: town.answer

## The realm's figures, where they're known (empty until the table is filled)

rule n7_fg_ruler
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.lore world.figure_ruler
cooldown 3d
say They say #world.figure_ruler# means to raise the levy again. | #world.figure_ruler# is to pass through, they say. They'll sweep the streets for once. | Do you think #world.figure_ruler# even knows our town's name?
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=figure 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_fg_lord
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.lore world.figure_lord
cooldown 3d
say #world.figure_lord# rode through with twenty riders. For what? | #world.figure_lord#'s steward was in the market, buying up the best of everything. | Our lord. #world.figure_lord#. Ever seen them? Me neither.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=figure 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_fg_captain
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.lore|talk.crime world.figure_captain
cooldown 3d
say #world.figure_captain# has doubled the night watch. Something's up. | They say #world.figure_captain# never sleeps. Just stands in a doorway and glares. | #world.figure_captain# had a watchman flogged for drinking. Fair, I suppose.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=figure 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_fg_high_priest
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.lore world.figure_high_priest
cooldown 3d
say #world.figure_high_priest# is to lead the prayers at the festival, they say. | They say #world.figure_high_priest# fasts a whole week every winter. | #world.figure_high_priest# wrote to every chapel. More candles, fewer excuses.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=figure 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_fg_hero
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.lore world.figure_hero
cooldown 3d
say Every pup in the street wants to be #world.figure_hero# when they're grown. | They sing about #world.figure_hero# in the tavern now. Badly. | Did #world.figure_hero# really do all that? Or is it the songs?
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=hero 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_fg_villain
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.lore|talk.bandits world.figure_villain
cooldown 3d
say Lock up tonight. They say #world.figure_villain# has been seen on the roads. | Mothers frighten their pups with #world.figure_villain# now. Works, too. | If #world.figure_villain# ever comes here, I'm hiding in the well.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=villain 1h
then other: town.answer

## The town's news, as it falls on each (world.*, newcomers, crime, news of their own)

rule n7_wd_wedding
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day world.wedding=recent
cooldown 3d
say Another wedding. The chapel's never had it so good. | Did you hear the wedding? I think the whole town heard the wedding. | Weddings, weddings. Somebody'll be marrying me off next.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=wedding 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_wd_birth
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day world.birth=recent
cooldown 3d
say A new pup in town. You can hear it from the well. | They've had the baby. A fine loud one, by the sound. | Another mouth. Good. The town needs pups.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=birth 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_wd_death
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day world.death=recent
cooldown 3d
say The bell was going a long while yesterday. | Another one buried. The town feels thinner. | They say the whole street turned out for the burying. Good. That's how it should be.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=death 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_wd_festival_levy
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.festival world.festival=soon
cooldown 3d
say They're paying for the festival lamps out of the levy, mind. | They're putting up bunting in the good streets. Ours get the leftover string. | Festival's coming. Every price in the market's gone up a paw's width already.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=festival 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_wd_festival_poor
when concept=talk.festival|talk.smalltalk world.festival=today self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say Feast for some, crumbs for the rest. | Free ale till noon, they said. I've been here since dawn and seen none of it. | I've no festival coat. I've a coat. It'll do.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=festival 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_wd_festival_rich
when concept=talk.festival|talk.smalltalk world.festival=today self.wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say Dreadful crush. One can't move for revellers. | We gave for the lamps, you know. Half of them. | My dressmaker's made me look like a cake. A festival cake. I'm told it's the fashion.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=festival 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_nc_heights
when concept=talk.newcomer self.wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say A newcomer? Where are they lodging? Not near us, I hope. | #topic.subject#. Do we know the family? | Is #topic.subject# anyone? I mean, anyone anyone?
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=newcomer 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_nc_warm
when concept=talk.newcomer self.warmth=warm
cooldown 2d
say We should take #topic.subject# something. A loaf. A pie. | It's hard, being new. I'll call on #topic.subject# tomorrow. | Someone should show #topic.subject# where the well is. And the honest baker.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=newcomer 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_nc_neighbours
when concept=talk.newcomer pair.neighbours=yes
cooldown 2d
say #topic.subject#'s taking the empty place on our row. | So we've a new neighbour. #topic.subject#. Heard them unpacking at midnight. | Have you met #topic.subject#? We'll hear them through the wall soon enough.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=newcomer 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_nc_guard
when concept=talk.newcomer self.role=guard
cooldown 2d
say I'll be keeping an eye on #topic.subject#. Nothing against them. Habit. | #topic.subject# came in through the gate with a cartload. Polite enough. | New faces mean new trouble, nine times in ten. The tenth's all right.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=newcomer 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_nc_old
when concept=talk.newcomer self.stage=old
cooldown 2d
say In my day you knew every face. Now look. #topic.subject#! Who's that? | Another new one. Soon there'll be nobody I know. | #topic.subject#. I'll learn the name, then they'll leave. They always leave.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=newcomer 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_nc_merchant
when concept=talk.newcomer self.role=merchant
cooldown 2d
say A new customer, I hope. #topic.subject#. Have they coin, do you know? | I'll send #topic.subject# a little something. First purchase half price. Second, full. | Every newcomer needs a pot, a broom and a blanket. I've all three.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=newcomer 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_cr_lock
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft|assault self.business!=none
cooldown 1d
say After #topic.victim#, I've put a second bar on the door. | I'm sleeping in the back room till they've caught whoever did #topic.victim#. | I've moved the takings since #topic.victim#. Don't ask me where.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=crime 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_cr_parent
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft|assault self.parent=yes self.age<=45
cooldown 1d
say After #topic.victim#, I've told the pups to come straight home. Straight home. | The little ones keep asking about #topic.victim#. What do I tell them? | I walked mine to the well this morning, after #topic.victim#. They thought I'd gone soft.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=crime 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_cr_night
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft|assault here.time=dusk|night
cooldown 1d
say I'll not walk home alone tonight, after #topic.victim#. | Every shadow's somebody tonight. Poor #topic.victim#. | Walk with me as far as the corner? Only after #topic.victim#...
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=crime 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_cr_arrest_short
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=arrest self.temper=short
cooldown 1d
say Good. Lock #topic.subject# up and lose the key. | About time the Watch earned their bread. | Hang them in the square, I say. Well. Lock them up.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=arrest 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_cr_arrest_warm
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=arrest self.warmth=warm
cooldown 1d
say Poor #topic.subject#. Whatever they did, there's a family. | I knew #topic.subject#'s mother. She'll be heartbroken. | Arrested. Gods. I hope they're fed in there.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=arrest 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_nw_work_poor
when concept=talk.news topic.kind=work self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say #topic.news#. Things are looking up, for once. | #topic.news#. We'll eat properly this winter. | #topic.news#. I could cry. I did cry, a little.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=goodnews 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_nw_marriage_neighbours
when concept=talk.news topic.kind=marriage pair.neighbours=yes
cooldown 2d
say #topic.news#. You'll have heard the wedding through the wall, I'm afraid. | #topic.news#. There'll be one more of us on the row now. | #topic.news#. There's cake left over. Come and help us with it.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=goodnews 1h
then other: town.answer

rule n7_nw_crime_neighbours
when concept=talk.news topic.kind=crime pair.neighbours=yes self.role!=guard
cooldown 2d
say #topic.news#. Right next door to you. Did you hear nothing? | #topic.news#. Lock your door tonight. I mean it. | #topic.news#. In our own street.
remember pair: on=answer 1h
remember pair: ans=crime_me 1h
then other: town.answer

## Answering a remark about the town's people and news (self answers; pair.mem.ans says what about; each
## remembers its stance, pair.mem.aa: chat, glad, grave, ask, pup)

rule n7_aa_plain
when concept=town.answer
say Is that so. | Hm. Sounds about right. | Well, well. | You don't say.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_plain2
when concept=town.answer
say #agree#. | So I heard. | Mm.

rule n7_aa_priest
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=priest
say A good soul, all told. | They mean well. They go on, but they mean well. | You could do worse for a priest.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_priest_devout
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=priest self.piety=devout
say A good soul. We're lucky in our priest. | I never miss a Restday. Not one in twenty years. | It does you good, a sermon. Even a long one.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_priest_ordinary
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=priest self.piety=ordinary
say I go for the singing. And the bread after. | I'll go Restday. Probably. Possibly. | I keep meaning to go. Then it's Restday and I'm asleep.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_flock
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=flock
say I've been meaning to come. My knees. | Restday. I'll be there. Near the back. | I know, I know. Work. Always work.
remember pair: aa=excuse 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_flock_devout
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=flock self.piety=devout
say I'll be there. I've not missed one I could help. | Bless you for asking. Truly. | I've been praying at home. It's not the same, I know.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_flock_poor
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=flock_poor
say Thank you. I might. | I'll not say no. Not this week. | You're kind. I'll come by after the bell.
remember pair: aa=glad 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_flock_poor_proud
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=flock_poor self.warmth=cold
say We're managing. | Give it to someone who needs it. | I'll not take the chapel's bread.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_to_priest
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=to_priest
say An hour, no more. Bring a cushion. | Come by the chapel after the bell. We'll talk. | The Bright One keep you, and your knees.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_shop
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=shop
say They're all the same, shopkeepers. Thumb on the scale. | Go elsewhere, then. Oh. There is nowhere else. | Mine's worse. Mine sells me last week's bread at this week's price.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_shop_merchant
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=shop self.role=merchant
say Try running a shop. Every penny's argued over. | Short weight? Never. Well. Not on purpose. | We're not the enemy, #address#. The carters are.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_shopgood
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=shopgood
say Good sort, that one. | You're lucky. Mine would charge you for the smile. | Hold on to a shopkeeper like that.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_keeper_to_customer
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=customer
say For you, aye. I'll put it by. | I'll see what I can do. | I might. If you ask nicely.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_keeper_price
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=customer_price
say Up again, I'm afraid. It's the roads. | Don't ask. I'll only cry. | Not this week. Next week, maybe.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_keeper_failing
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=customer|customer_price self.business=failing
say Anything you want. Anything. Please. | Name your price. Go on. Anything. | You're the first through the door all day.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_customer_miss
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=keeper_miss
say I've been busy, that's all. | Never! I'd not go anywhere else. | Money's tight, that's all. It's not you.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_customer_reply
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=keeper
say I'll come by later. | You know me too well. | Go on, then. What is it?
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_customer_poor
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=keeper|keeper_miss self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Nothing for me this week. I'm #skint#. | I've been going without. It's not you. | I'll look. I'll not buy, but I'll look.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_leader
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=leader|leader_house|figure
say The great don't think of us. Why should we think of them? | Their business. Not mine. | I'd like a day in their boots. Just one.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_leader_poor
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=leader|figure self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Whatever it is, it'll cost us. | Must be nice, being them. | And not one of them's ever been down our street.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_leader_house
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=leader|leader_house self.house
say Careful. You're talking about the family. | Stern, but fair. Mostly. | I'd not say that where the steward can hear.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_figure_young
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=figure|hero self.stage=young|adolescent
say Have you seen them? Really seen them? | I'm going to meet them one day. | Are they tall? I bet they're tall.
remember pair: aa=pup 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_hero
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=hero
say Half of it's true. That's still a lot. | Good. We could do with a few like that. | I'd buy them a drink, if they ever came in.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_villain
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=villain
say Don't. I'll be up all night listening. | Let them try it here. | The Watch'll have them. Sooner or later.
remember pair: aa=grave 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_villain_young
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=villain self.stage=young|adolescent
say I'm not scared. I'm not. | Would they eat me? | I'd fight them. With a stick.
remember pair: aa=pup 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_neighbour
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=neighbour
say Every row has one. | Better that than the other sort. | Mine sings. At dawn. Every dawn.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_neighbourgood
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=neighbourgood
say You're lucky. Hold on to that one. | A good neighbour's worth more than a good roof. | Mine wouldn't lend me a candle.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_wedding
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=wedding|goodnews
say Good. There's not enough of that. | Lovely. I do like good news. | Here's to that.
remember pair: aa=glad 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_wedding_widowed
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=wedding self.widowed=yes
say Lovely. I was married in that chapel. A long time ago. | Good. Let them be happy while they can. | I went. Sat at the back. It was lovely.
remember pair: aa=glad 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_wedding_dry
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=wedding self.humour=dry
say Give it a year. | Love's grand. So's a sound roof. | Weddings: the town's way of getting a free meal out of you.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_birth
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=birth
say Good. The town needs pups. | Loud ones are healthy, my mother said. | Bless it. Bless the mother more.
remember pair: aa=glad 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_birth_parent
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=birth self.parent=yes
say They'll not sleep for a year. I remember. | Lovely. I'll send round our old cradle. | Ah. Enjoy it while they're small. They don't stay small.
remember pair: aa=glad 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_death
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=death
say It comes for us all. | I'll go to the burying. | The town'll be the poorer.
remember pair: aa=grave 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_death_mourning
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=death self.mourning=kin|friend
priority 1
say Don't. I've had my own this week. | Every bell, I think it's for mine. | I can't talk about burying. Not now.
remember pair: aa=grave 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_festival
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=festival
say Still. A festival's a festival. | Ah, let them have their fun. Let us have ours. | I'll dance anyway. Nobody can levy that.
remember pair: aa=glad 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_festival_merry
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=festival self.humour=merry
say I'll dance with you. I'll dance with anyone. | Free ale? Did somebody say free ale? | I've been practising my singing. Hide.
remember pair: aa=glad 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_newcomer
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=newcomer
say Give them a week. We'll see. | Seems decent enough. | New faces. The town needs them.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_newcomer_cold
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=newcomer self.warmth=cold
say I'll wait and see. | Newcomers come and go. | Let them prove themselves.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_newcomer_incomer
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=newcomer self.from=frosthollow|coldwater|oakhaven|mirebridge|larkfield|southmeadow here.region=ridgemere
say I was new once. Nobody brought me a pie. | Be kind. I remember my first winter here. | They'll learn. Took me three years to stop getting lost.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_crime
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=crime
say Lock your doors. I'm locking mine. | It's getting worse. Every season. | Nobody's safe. Not even in the good streets.
remember pair: aa=grave 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_crime_guard
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=crime|crime_me self.role=guard
say We're on it. Give us a day. | I'll ask about. Someone always saw something. | Tell your street: anything odd, come to the Watch.
remember pair: aa=grave 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_crime_sump
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=crime self.quarter=sump here.region=ridgemere
say And they'll come knocking down our way. You'll see. | Never the Heights they search. Never. | Wasn't us. It's never us. Somehow it's always us.
remember pair: aa=grave 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_crime_nervy
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=crime|crime_me self.temper=nervy
say I'll not sleep tonight. | I've put a chair against my door. Two chairs. | What if they come back? What if they come to ours?
remember pair: aa=grave 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_crime_me
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=crime_me
say Gods! Are you hurt? | What did they take? | I'm so sorry. Did you see them?
remember pair: aa=ask 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_arrest
when concept=town.answer pair.mem.ans=arrest
say What did they do, do you know? | They'll be out by Restday, I'd bet. | The gaol's no place to get better.
remember pair: aa=grave 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_dry
when concept=town.answer self.humour=dry pair.mem.ans=shop|neighbour|leader|figure|festival|newcomer|hero
say Riveting. | The town never sleeps. Worse luck. | And the world keeps turning.
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

rule n7_aa_merry
when concept=town.answer self.humour=merry pair.mem.ans=shop|neighbour|leader|figure|festival|wedding|newcomer|goodnews|birth|hero
say Ha! This town. | Never a dull day. | You do hear things, don't you!
remember pair: aa=chat 1h
then other: town.close

## The last word on the town's people and news (pair.mem.aa says how it was taken)

rule n7_close_ans
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=answer
say Aye. Well. That's the town. | So it goes. | Hm. We'll see. | There's always something.

rule n7_close_ans_grave
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=answer pair.mem.aa=grave
priority 1
say Aye. Bad times. | Gods keep us. | Strange times. | Mind how you go.

rule n7_close_ans_glad
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=answer pair.mem.aa=glad
say Good times, for once. | We'll drink to it. | Something to smile about.

rule n7_close_ans_excuse
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=answer pair.mem.aa=excuse
say I'll hold you to that. | Near the back's still in the chapel. | I'll keep a place for you.

rule n7_close_ans_ask
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=answer pair.mem.aa=ask
say I'm all right. Shaken, that's all. | Everything I had on me. | It was too dark. I'd not know them again. | I'll live. That's the main thing.

rule n7_close_ans_pup
when concept=town.close pair.mem.on=answer pair.mem.aa=pup
say Maybe one day. | Ha. You and every pup in town. | Off you go, now.
